{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1314317-different-editions-of-the-books-of-the-wyrm","id":1314317,"title":"Different editions of the Books of the Wyrm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-25T10:18:50-07:00","id":1314317,"title":"Different editions of the Books of the Wyrm","content":"Are there big changes between 1st ed Book of the Wyrm, 2nd ed Book of the Wyrm, and W20 Book of the Wyrm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T12:15:25-07:00","id":1314338,"title":"","content":"20th edition is basically a total overhaul of the BSDs. As the White Howlers in 20th edition are very diufferent, the BSD goals are very different as well. They are still horrid mauling things, but now some believe the apocalypse has been won.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T17:13:19-07:00","id":1314406,"title":"","content":"In addition to the aforementioned changes Book of the Wyrm 20th also has a lot of new material that cannot be found on the previous editions. Like information on other Fallen shifters aside from BSD\u2019s and Buzzards, 20th also has the Antara, Histpah, Mnetics, Bitter-Grins, the Mad Destroyers, Balefire Sharks and the Xibalan. It also introduced some new Wyrm Critters the Mockeries whom consist of War Wolves, Anurana, Samsa, Kerasi and Yeren. It also has information on the Chulorviah who were first introduced in Blood Dimmed Tides.<br /> <br /> All in all if your going to get one Book of the Wyrm it should be the 20th Anniversary edition.<br /> <br /> Edit: I also recommend the Storytellers Vault product Riot of the Flesh by Holden that has more Fomori Breeds for 20th edition and more about playing Fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 05-25-2019, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T10:17:02-07:00","id":1314553,"title":"","content":"W20 Book of Wyrm doesn't have stats for Wyrm champions and that makes realy sad. While 1st edition had an awesome First Ronin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T13:18:10-07:00","id":1314581,"title":"","content":"Only First book of the Wyrm had the Dancer Renown Creeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T08:17:42-07:00","id":1314706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1314317-different-editions-of-the-books-of-the-wyrm?p=1314553#post1314553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 Book of Wyrm doesn't have stats for Wyrm champions and that makes realy sad. While 1st edition had an awesome First Ronin.</div> </div> </div> </div>First Ronin is awesome and leaves a lot, early books always give stats for Badass.<br /> <br /> And To be honest I think early books Always do something... stupid, giving stats for Badass, making out-of-control crossovers, giving very strange stats. But it doesn't matter, early things are always imperfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-27-2019, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T11:21:32-07:00","id":1314740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1314317-different-editions-of-the-books-of-the-wyrm?p=1314706#post1314706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First Ronin is awesome and leaves a lot, early books always give stats for Badass.<br /> <br /> And To be honest I think early books Always do something... stupid, giving stats for Badass, making out-of-control crossovers, giving very strange stats. But it doesn't matter, early things are always imperfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>No supplement is perfect and I find it exciting that older supplements have things that newer ones don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T15:38:11-07:00","id":1314818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1314317-different-editions-of-the-books-of-the-wyrm?p=1314740#post1314740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No supplement is perfect and I find it exciting that older supplements have things that newer ones don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah for instance Samuel-Haight, one statted Incarna in mage Book of Madness, older books also have better ideas...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T18:30:42-07:00","id":1316347,"title":"","content":"A lot of RPGs from the very early 90s, including first editions of Vampire, Werewolf and Mage, were rather different animals from what came later. I think a lot of this was that the heavy influence of AD&amp;D and similar games, were just about everything was fully started out. (Including gods, for those that wanted to have their PCs try to fight Odin or Zeus.) Sort of the way early Ravenloft had stats for all the Darklords, even though from a genre standpoint, actually fighting one of them to the death was rather improbable. <br /> <br /> I was always a little disappointed that revised didn't have a Book of the Wyrm Companion that included a bunch of new stuff (more Banes and the like, more Fomori breeds, more Wyrm cults, etc.). But then I was also disappointed that Subsidiaries wasn't a series of four or five volumes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T23:32:01-07:00","id":1316382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1314317-different-editions-of-the-books-of-the-wyrm?p=1316347#post1316347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was always a little disappointed that revised didn't have a Book of the Wyrm Companion that included a bunch of new stuff (more Banes and the like, more Fomori breeds, more Wyrm cults, etc.). But then I was also disappointed that Subsidiaries wasn't a series of four or five volumes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't say?<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1173822-pentex-research-inspiration-company-by-company\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...any-by-company</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T00:31:29-07:00","id":1316389,"title":"","content":"Is it that obvious?<br /> <br /> I would've at least liked a second one covering O'Tolley's (it would touch on a lot of things that impact the Garou and Fera in negative ways such as cattle ranching, food and paper waste, humanity being separated from nature in such a key area as food, kinkolk health, etc.), Herculean (gamers love guns, especially in a combat heavy game like Werewolf), OMNI (a threat for more tech oriented characters, plus some crossover potential), Hallahan (a potential major threat for the Rokea), Harold &amp; Harold (a lot of potential BSD involvement), and Young &amp; Smith (because they are <i>everywhere</i> and would possibly allowed for a modern look at the Red Circle).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T15:42:53-07:00","id":1322841,"title":"","content":"My biggest gripe (and really only gripe) with 20th was they nixed the white howler based bsd camp. Y\u2019all know the one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T18:24:11-07:00","id":1324318,"title":"","content":"The Cluithi are awesome. If we weren't still using second edition info, I'd be missing them too. Book of the Wyrm 1st and 2nd edition is more crossover-friendly, if that's your thing. There's information on Dancer Ronin in both 1st edition (page 15, paragraph 5, sentence 1 ) and 2nd edition (page 90, paragraph 1, sentence 1.)<br /> <br /> Get the MET book! It has totems and rites that never made it into the rest of the books! Two totems and 23 rites -- some of which are corrupt Gaian rites, others are Dancr-specific. The back of the book has early information on Fallen Fera, later updated in Wyrm 20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}